11 November 2026, Android 17 / API 37, Go QA 8087405 and isolated PostgreSQL 18.
LocalBackendCoreTest#accessTokenExpiresOnItsOwnAndOneRefreshRestoresTheRequest

The test read the signed access claims and verified exp − iat = 900 seconds.
GET /me returned 200 before expiry. The emulator waited 903564 ms of wall time.
At expiry the observed request statuses were 401, 200. The Go log also records
HTTP 200 for the refresh between those two attempts.
The app retained the same account and session epoch. The credential revision
increased once and the signed-in workspace remained available.

Instrumentation: Time: 918.486; OK (1 test).
PostgreSQL after test logout: generation=2, refresh_tokens=2, used_tokens=1.
